        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Stench"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(aura, olfactory)\n\n10 feet. A creature entering the aura or starting its turn there must succeed at a DC 34 Fortitude save or become sickened 1 (plus slowed 1 as long as it's sickened on a critical failure). While within the aura, the creature takes a \u20132 circumstance penalty to saves against disease and to recover from the sickened condition. A creature that succeeds at its save is temporarily immune for 1 minute."
            },
            "id": "bb619c81-371e-4040-84fb-aa89cb56e8f7",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-17T12:41:22.444580"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Lazurite-Infused Flesh"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "Falrok's flesh is infused with lazurite, and he gains the benefits undead creatures gain from this mineral at all times. When in an area infused with lazurite, such as the Sanctum of the Starved, these benefits increase to a +3 circumstance bonus to saving throws against positive effects. This infusion also grants Falrok his resistance to positive damage."
            },
            "id": "15762c1d-1028-4710-b50b-f8d83e7311a7",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-17T12:41:22.444580"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Ghast Fever"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(disease, virulent); DC 34 Fortitude; Stage 1: carrier with no ill effect (1 day); Stage 2: 4d8 negative damage and regains half as many Hit Points from all healing (1 day); Stage 3: 4d8 negative damage and gains no benefit from healing (1 day); Stage 4: dead, and rises as a ghast the next midnight. ()"
            },
            "id": "73bc58bd-12de-41ae-8ec4-3935226501ba",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-17T12:41:22.444580"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Paralysis"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(incapacitation, occult, necromancy)\n\nAny living creature hit by Falrok's attack must succeed at a DC 34 Fortitude save or become paralyzed.\n\nIt can attempt a new save at the end of each of its turns, and the DC cumulatively decreases by 1 on each such save."
            },
            "id": "255afe0b-54f2-4ff6-ae57-d51146d6b0c0",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-17T12:41:22.444580"
